Toy Town Rush Hour — independently assembled GPT recreation.
Authored with GPT-6.1 Sol, high reasoning effort.
Original reference: Lemomo / LemoLab, lemo-opuscar (MIT), https://lemomo-ai.github.io/lemo-opuscar/films/tilt-shift.mp4

Attributed generic style/render components (MIT):
styles/tilt-shift/demo/geo.js — generic merged boxes, faces, cylinders, disks and rings.
styles/tilt-shift/demo/city.js — buildingMaterial() facade shader and its shared sky/light uniforms only. buildCity() is never called.
styles/tilt-shift/demo/traffic.js — makeFleet() vehicle mesh instancer and makeTrails() light-ribbon renderer only. Original simulation, lanes, signal/crowd scene choreography are not called.
styles/tilt-shift/demo/sky.js — generic clock-to-daylight/environment system.
styles/tilt-shift/demo/post.js — generic supersampled tilt-band/physical DOF, GTAO, bloom and grade.
core/lib.js — generic deterministic math.
Original main.js, story.js, ducks.js and train.js are not runtime dependencies. All town assembly, train/duck geometry, acting, traffic choreography, camera application, UI and score are newly authored in this directory. Published road/camera dimensions and cue times are reference measurements, preserved to match the original staging.

Overpass and Overpass Mono: Delve Withrington, Dave Bailey, Thomas Jockin / Red Hat, SIL OFL 1.1. Fresh local font downloads from Google Fonts:
